From ef48558d2488a3998e9eac1bfb852fc7e18aadcc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mark-vis <118430440+mark-vis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 06:12:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 11/14] latex-lab: label contract, caption/separator,
 in-paragraph labels

latex-lab-float documents the contract of the socket caption/label
(argument, used more than once, no side effects, output is the content
of Lbl) and adds the socket caption/separator (no argument, used after
caption/label/end and para/begin, so its output belongs to the caption
text). The default plugs give the output of before (caption/label
kernel: colon and space inside Lbl; caption/separator kernel: empty);
the plugs label-only and colon put the colon outside Lbl. Code that
suppresses the label must void caption/separator as well: \caption* in
\@makecaption and the listings titles (latex-lab-listings) do.

A label that typesets nothing (the plug noop of caption/label, or a
label of size zero, as measured by \@makecaption) gets the plugs nolabel
of the label tagging sockets, as \caption* does: no empty Lbl, and a
wide caption gets one P instead of unbalanced para hooks (fixes
latex3/latex2e#2022). This keeps the structure of \@makecaption; the
sketch in #2022, which moves the label tagging sockets into the socket
caption/label, would change the contract of caption/label and is left
to that issue.

The label tagging sockets caption/label/begin and caption/label/end
can also be used inside the caption paragraph (as the caption package
does): if a marked content chunk is open, the chunk is interrupted for
the label and continued after it, and the label becomes a child of the
paragraph structure. The plugs nolabel then do nothing. An open chunk
alone does not show this, because a caption can be in a box inside
another paragraph (threeparttable puts the table into a \vtop after
\noindent). So caption/begin records the number of the caption
structure, and the label is taken as inside the paragraph only if a
chunk is open and the current structure is not the caption structure.
This needs nothing from the code that uses the sockets, so a class with
its own \@makecaption (the recipe documented below) works in such boxes
as well. lttagging documents the second use.

The begindocument code that redefines \@makecaption keeps its label
latex-lab-testphase-float, now given explicitly and documented:
acmart, asmejour, asmeconf and mitthesis remove the code by this name.
A voids rule is the documented way to keep an own \@makecaption.

New latex-lab tests: float-021 (plugs, a class plug, label inside the
paragraph), float-022 (separator outside Lbl, listings titles,
\caption*), float-025 and float-026 (regression tests for the label of
the begindocument code: \RemoveFromHook and a voids rule keep a class
\@makecaption, also for \caption*), float-027 (captions of latex-lab in
a \vtop inside a paragraph, as threeparttable), float-029 (the same
with a class \@makecaption) and float-030 (an empty label, #2022).
